1. Definitions and scope

Licensor means a rights holder making material available under this license.
Each Licensor grants only rights it owns or is authorized to grant.

Software means the first-party FlyCut Caption source code, documentation and
other materials distributed under this license, including its React library,
desktop application and first-party sidecar code. Material carrying separate
license notices remains governed by those notices.

Covered Work means the Software, modifications to it, and a combined program
incorporating Software code by copying, linking, embedding or bundling it as
an integrated part. Mere aggregation of independent programs does not make
an independent program a Covered Work.

Corresponding Source means the preferred source form for modifying a Covered
Work, including modifications, interface definitions, and the scripts and
instructions necessary to build, install and run it. It excludes user media,
credentials, private user data, independent general-purpose tools, and
unmodified system libraries. Do not include secrets in source distributions.

Closed-Source Integration means incorporating Software into a Covered Work
while withholding any Corresponding Source required by this license, offering
the Covered Work under incompatible proprietary terms, or seeking exemption
from the source-sharing requirements in section 4. An independent program
that only communicates through an ordinary API, CLI or MCP interface, without
incorporating Software code or constituting a Covered Work, is not such an
integration solely because its own source is private.

2. Community permission

Subject to all conditions below, each Licensor grants you a worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free copyright license to use, copy, study, modify,
and distribute the Software and Covered Works, and operate them as services.
Personal, educational, internal-business and commercial use, including
charging for compliant copies or services, is permitted.

This permission is conditional on sections 3, 4 and 5. You may not sublicense
a Covered Work under inconsistent terms. Recipients receive these community
permissions directly from the relevant Licensors, subject to this license.

3. Product name, branding and notices

You must retain the product name "FlyCut Caption" for the Software and its
modified versions. You must not rename the Software or a Covered Work,
substitute another product identity for it, or remove, obscure or replace
existing FlyCut Caption product-name, logo or attribution notices in its
user interface or distributed documentation. These requirements apply to
private modifications, distributions and hosted deployments alike.

Existing interface product-name and branding notices must remain readily
visible in their normal locations. If no user interface exists, identify
FlyCut Caption in distributed documentation and existing version/help
identification, if any. Preserve copyright and license notices, this license,
and applicable third-party legal notices in copies and distributions.

You may add your operator name and "Unofficial modified version by [operator]"
alongside, but not in place of, FlyCut Caption's identity. Modified or
third-party-operated versions must clearly identify their changes or
operator and must not imply official endorsement. A fork's technical
repository URL, package namespace or build ID may change to avoid collisions,
but may not replace the required product identity. An independent host
application may keep its own name, but must not conceal or replace the
identity of incorporated FlyCut Caption software.

This license grants only the limited branding display permission needed to
comply with this section. It does not authorize official-status claims,
endorsement, partnership, or branding unrelated products as FlyCut. It does
not require watermarks or branding on users' output videos or subtitles.

4. Source availability

When distributing source code of a Covered Work, include its Corresponding
Source, this license and notices identifying modifications. License your
modifications to recipients under this same community license.

When distributing a Covered Work in executable or bundled form, provide
recipients its complete Corresponding Source under this license at no
additional charge. A prominent, working download link to source for the exact
version may be used. Maintain access while offering the executable or bundle
for download. A different or unmodified upstream version is insufficient
for your modifications.

If users interact remotely over a network with a modified Covered Work you
operate, prominently offer those users the Corresponding Source of that
version under this license without charge. Maintain the offer while that
version is operated. Make the offer reachable through its interface or, for
API-only services, accompanying service documentation. This includes internal
users of a modified network service.

Private modifications neither distributed nor made available for remote
interaction do not require publication of source, but remain subject to
name retention and the Closed-Source Integration rule. Source-sharing does
not extend to independent programs merely communicating with a Covered Work
as described in section 1.

5. Closed-source integration and commercial permission

The community permission does not authorize Closed-Source Integration,
including private Closed-Source Integration. Before such integration, obtain
a separate written commercial license from FlyCut Team covering the relevant
rights, code, versions and intended use. Hosted-service payments, support
purchases, or quotes are not commercial software license grants.

FlyCut Team may license only rights it owns or is authorized to offer.
Third-party obligations cannot be waived without the relevant rights holder's
permission. See COMMERCIAL-LICENSE.md; contact x007xyzabc@gmail.com.

Commercial integration permission does not automatically permit renaming,
brand removal or official-endorsement claims. Any exception to section 3
must be explicitly granted in writing by the relevant rights holder.

6. Media outputs and independent programs

Processing user-supplied videos, audio, subtitles or other content does not
change their ownership or licensing. You may create, publish and sell such
outputs without a commercial software license, unless their content itself
incorporates covered Software material. Users remain responsible for rights
in input content.

Ordinary business use or independent API, CLI or MCP calls do not by
themselves require a commercial integration license. They do not exempt the
Software deployment from branding or applicable source-sharing requirements.

7. Third-party material and earlier grants

Third-party code, models, fonts, media and binaries retain their own licenses.
This license neither replaces them nor grants rights a Licensor does not
control. Comply with applicable third-party terms for your distribution
and deployment.

This license applies to revisions expressly released under it. It does not
revoke or replace permissions already granted for earlier copies. Historical
licenses kept for reference do not alternatively license this revision.

8. Termination

Your permissions terminate automatically if you materially violate these
conditions. Stop the violating use or distribution and contact the relevant
Licensor to resolve the violation. Reinstatement requires that Licensor's
written confirmation. Compliant downstream recipients do not lose their
permissions solely because of your violation. Termination does not affect
rights granted by a separate applicable agreement.

